-- Search the web using Exa AI - performs real-time web searches and can scrape content from specific URLs
-- Provides up-to-date information for current events and recent data
-- Supports configurable result counts and returns the content from the most relevant websites
-- Use this tool for accessing information beyond knowledge cutoff
-- Searches are performed automatically within a single API call
+- Search the web for up-to-date information: news, current events, recent releases, prices, and anything beyond your knowledge cutoff
+- STRONGLY PREFER this tool over webfetch for research / news / "what's happening" style questions — it discovers relevant sources for you; do NOT guess URLs and webfetch them
+- Returns a ranked result list (title, URL, snippet, publish time when available), sometimes with a short direct answer
+- Follow up with webfetch on a specific result URL when you need the full page content
 
 Usage notes:
-  - Supports live crawling modes: 'fallback' (backup if cached unavailable) or 'preferred' (prioritize live crawling)
-  - Search types: 'auto' (balanced), 'fast' (quick results), 'deep' (comprehensive search)
-  - Configurable context length for optimal LLM integration
-  - Domain filtering and advanced search options available
+  - depth: 'basic' (default, fast and cheap) or 'advanced' (more thorough, costs more credits — use sparingly)
+  - timeRange: restrict results to the last 'day' | 'week' | 'month' | 'year' — use it for time-sensitive queries
+  - Keep queries short and keyword-focused; issue multiple searches for multi-faceted questions
 
 The current year is {{year}}. You MUST use this year when searching for recent information or current events
 - Example: If the current year is 2026 and the user asks for "latest AI news", search for "AI news 2026", NOT "AI news 2025"
